i should have been more explicit ...
let's say you have a gem inventory:
a - 17 white gems
b - 3 white gems
c - 2 white gems
d - a white gem
and you enter an assorted antiques shop and drop 1 of each. the
shopkeeper probably won't be interested in "a" (above) so you #name "a"
"worthless white" or something. dropping "b" you find that you get 525
gold pieces, so you name "b" "525 white" and so on with "c" and "d".
note that you are not #naming a particular gem but rather #naming
(calling) all gems of this kind a certain name. the next time that you
see a white gem, if it is one you've "discovered" it will be described
as you named it else it will appear as a white gem.

there's is a catch to this method as the prices may change over a long
enough period of time because shopkeepers discriminate...

